1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,910
After the 2010 earthquake,

2
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:05,076
the American Red Cross raised four hundred

3
00:00:05,126 --> 00:00:08,317
and eighty-eight million dollars for Haiti,

4
00:00:08,367 --> 00:00:10,578
and built six permanent homes.

5
00:00:10,628 --> 00:00:12,764
Disaster funds make promises.

6
00:00:12,814 --> 00:00:14,950
Almost nobody can check them.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,269
Taiwan has lived the same loop.

8
00:00:17,319 --> 00:00:18,691
In Hualien in 2024,

9
00:00:18,741 --> 00:00:24,002
almost eight hundred million Taiwan dollars were donated to the county.

10
00:00:24,052 --> 00:00:28,117
Eleven months later, sixteen percent had been paid out,

11
00:00:28,167 --> 00:00:31,933
and its committee had no affected households on it.

12
00:00:31,983 --> 00:00:34,775
After disputes over earlier donations,

13
00:00:34,825 --> 00:00:40,237
most people gave to the national foundation instead, about twice as much.

14
00:00:40,287 --> 00:00:42,257
People did not stop giving.

15
00:00:42,307 --> 00:00:44,950
They stopped trusting where it goes.

16
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,360
In 2025 a barrier lake flooded Guangfu.

17
00:00:47,410 --> 00:00:52,366
The national relief foundation publishes every transfer, which is more than most.

18
00:00:52,416 --> 00:00:54,776
Of 1.2 billion Taiwan dollars paid out,

19
00:00:54,826 --> 00:00:59,287
nearly ninety-nine percent was pre-allocated, most of it to one ministry.

20
00:00:59,337 --> 00:01:02,006
In eleven monthly reports, for eight months,

21
00:01:02,056 --> 00:01:05,776
not one more pre-allocated dollar was reported as reconciled.

22
00:01:05,826 --> 00:01:08,310
Pre-allocating is normal in an emergency.

23
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:13,377
The problem is what comes next: after the first hand, the public sees only totals,

24
00:01:13,427 --> 00:01:17,950
and households have no public way to confirm or dispute their own payment.

25
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,648
This is Kept, on a simulated version of the same disaster.

26
00:01:21,698 --> 00:01:24,261
Every hand acknowledges what it receives.

27
00:01:24,311 --> 00:01:26,429
When the ministry pays households,

28
00:01:26,479 --> 00:01:29,935
it publishes each payment as a line with no name on it.

29
00:01:29,985 --> 00:01:34,526
A household, verified by both the village chief and the township office,

30
00:01:34,576 --> 00:01:39,690
finds its own line without asking anyone, and says 'received', or 'not received'.

31
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:42,495
The custodian cannot sign for the household,

32
00:01:42,545 --> 00:01:45,236
and cannot pad the list without it showing.

33
00:01:45,286 --> 00:01:47,850
And because many households never answer,

34
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:52,950
the contract draws a random sample that an independent auditor visits in person.

35
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,553
An NGO can check eligibility on the spot with a zero-knowledge proof.

36
00:01:58,603 --> 00:02:03,668
The proof tells the NGO only that this is an eligible household

37
00:02:03,718 --> 00:02:08,540
that has not claimed yet; the NGO never receives the roster,

38
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:11,950
and the same household cannot claim twice.

39
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,529
The fund's charter is fixed when the money is raised.

40
00:02:17,579 --> 00:02:20,792
Spending outside it is refused.

41
00:02:20,842 --> 00:02:29,529
Changes wait in public, and the people the money is for can veto them, anonymously,

42
00:02:29,579 --> 00:02:31,950
one vote per household.

43
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,054
Why a blockchain?

44
00:02:33,104 --> 00:02:37,340
Because the people being overseen should not keep the only ledger,

45
00:02:37,390 --> 00:02:41,106
and several independent custodians need one shared record.

46
00:02:41,156 --> 00:02:44,158
Names, IDs and bank accounts never go on-chain.

47
00:02:44,208 --> 00:02:45,911
It works under today's law,

48
00:02:45,961 --> 00:02:48,444
and at Guangfu's scale it costs about a

49
00:02:48,494 --> 00:02:51,950
hundred and fifty to fifteen hundred dollars on-chain.

50
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:57,602
Two promises: how the money is used, and that no one is left out.

51
00:02:57,652 --> 00:02:59,950
Kept makes both verifiable.

